<title>USA: Clinton to discuss U.S. employment data.</title>
<headline>Clinton to discuss U.S. employment data.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-08-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>President Clinton will discuss the latest  U.S. employment data during an exchange with reporters at the White  House about 11 a.m. EDT (1500 GMT) on Friday, the White House announced.</p>
<p>Clinton will make his remarks in the Rose Garden, the White House  said.</p>
<p>Earlier Friday, the government said the nation's jobless rate dropped  back to a 24-year low of 4.8 percent last month as the economy produced  new jobs at an unexpectedly strong pace.</p>
</text>
